# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values before running locally or deploying.

# Postgres connection strings. If you're using Neon (e.g. via Vercel's Storage
# integration), it gives you both of these automatically — DATABASE_URL is the
# pooled connection the app uses at runtime, DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED is the direct
# connection Prisma uses to sync the schema (see the "build" script).
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require"
DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED="postgresql://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require"

# Password for the /admin dispatch dashboard. Change this before you go live.
ADMIN_PASSWORD="change-me"

# Shown in page titles, header, footer, etc. Set this to your real brand name.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_NAME="LoveMeAfter"

# Phone number customers can call/text, shown in the header and footer.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPPORT_PHONE="(555) 555-0100"

# The legal entity that contracts with customers, and the address a customer
# can post a cancellation to. Both appear on the service agreement
# (/agreement/<token>). The address is not optional if you sell at doors:
# California requires the cancellation notice to say where to send it, and a
# notice without an address is defective. The agreement says so in red until
# this is set.
NEXT_PUBLIC_LEGAL_ENTITY=""
NEXT_PUBLIC_BUSINESS_ADDRESS=""

# Doorstep deposits (see /admin/knock and docs/door-knock.md).
#
# The Venmo handle money is sent to, with or without the @, and the phone
# number Apple Cash is sent to inside Messages. Both are used to build the QR
# the customer scans; leave one blank and that payment method simply shows no
# code, which is a bad afternoon on a doorstep — set them before you knock.
# Apple Cash goes to its own number, not the support line — a payment landing
# in the middle of a booking call is a payment that gets missed.
NEXT_PUBLIC_VENMO_HANDLE="LOVEMEAFTER-Improvements"
NEXT_PUBLIC_APPLE_CASH_PHONE=""

# Google Ads: set these once you create the account/campaign and it'll start
# firing a "conversion" event whenever a booking is submitted. Leave both
# blank and nothing loads — safe to deploy without them.
# Ads ID looks like "AW-123456789", conversion label like "AbC-D_efG-h123"
# (Google Ads > Goals > Conversions > your action > "Tag setup" > "Install manually").
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ADS_ID=""
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ADS_CONVERSION_LABEL=""

# Optional: GA4 measurement ID ("G-XXXXXXXXXX") if you also want analytics
# alongside Ads. Uses the same script tag, independent of the two vars above.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=""

# --- Notifications: email/text for you, your customers, and your drivers ---
#
# These two blocks (RESEND_API_KEY/TWILIO_*) power every automated message
# in the app — src/lib/notify.ts. With none of them set, everything still
# saves fine (bookings, applications, status changes) — you just have to
# check /admin to see any of it. Set either block (or both; they're
# independent per-message, not just independent of each other) to turn on:
#   - you: a new booking or application, the instant it comes in
#   - the customer: a booking receipt, "your crew is confirmed" once you
#     assign a driver, a reminder the day before, a thank-you/review ask
#     once the job's marked Completed
#   - the driver: a text the moment you assign them a job in /admin (drivers
#     only get texts — the roster has phone numbers, not emails)
#
# Email, via Resend (resend.com — free tier, no credit card to start).
# Dashboard > API Keys > create one, with "Sending access" (not "Full
# access" — this key only ever needs to send).
RESEND_API_KEY=""
# Where YOUR alerts go. Also has to be the address you signed up to Resend
# with, unless NOTIFY_FROM_EMAIL below is set — see that var.
NOTIFY_EMAIL=""
# Resend's shared sandbox sender (used when this is blank) only delivers to
# the address that owns the Resend account — fine for NOTIFY_EMAIL above,
# but it means customer- and driver-facing email goes nowhere until you
# verify your own sending domain in Resend and set this to an address on it,
# e.g. "LoveMeAfter <bookings@lovemeafter.com>". Texting (below) has no such
# limit, so it's the one channel that reaches customers/drivers out of the box.
NOTIFY_FROM_EMAIL=""
#
# Text message, via Twilio (twilio.com — needs a phone number, a few
# dollars/month). Console > Account SID + Auth Token, plus the number you
# bought (TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER). NOTIFY_PHONE is where YOUR alerts go (your
# cell); customers and drivers get texted at the number already on their
# booking/application/driver record. All numbers in E.164 format, e.g.
# "+19165551234".
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=""
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=""
TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER=""
NOTIFY_PHONE=""
#
# A review link (Google Business, Yelp, whatever you use) dropped into the
# "thanks for booking" message sent once a job is marked Completed. Leave
# blank and that message still sends, just without the ask.
REVIEW_URL=""
#
# Wakes the app once a day to text/email customers whose move is tomorrow
# (src/app/api/cron/reminders, scheduled in vercel.json). Any long random
# string — this is what proves a request coming into that route is actually
# Vercel's cron and not someone hitting the URL directly to spam your
# customers. Required for the reminder cron to do anything; everything else
# in the app works fine without it.
CRON_SECRET=""
#
# Only needed if the site's production domain isn't what Vercel already
# knows about (rare) — overrides the link the reminder cron builds for
# "manage your booking". Every other manage-link/confirmation-link path
# reads the real request instead and needs no configuration here.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=""

# --- Maps: address autocomplete, geocoding, and driving distance ---
#
# The booking page works with none of these set. Accuracy improves as you add
# one; the code picks the best key available and needs no other changes.
#
# BEST — Google Maps Platform. The same address data Uber and Lugg use.
# Requires a Google Cloud account with billing enabled (there is no keyless
# tier). Enable these three APIs on the key: Places API, Geocoding API,
# Directions API. Then restrict the key to your domain before going live —
# an unrestricted key can be lifted off your site and billed to you.
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=""
#
# GOOD — Mapbox. Also needs a signup, generous free tier.
MAPBOX_TOKEN=""
#
# With neither key set, the site uses free keyless services and still works:
#   - US Census geocoder for resolving typed addresses (no signup, and its
#     TIGER/Line street data is genuinely good at US house numbers)
#   - Photon for the autocomplete dropdown (weaker US coverage — this is the
#     part that improves most from a key)
#   - OSRM for driving distance
#   - a built-in table of service-area town centres as a last resort, so a
#     trip always maps even when everything upstream is unreachable
